["er.request/1",{"definition_version":1,"fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-36273a6f1c4e3567972b93817b8d502ed231a4ccac1c012b7a2422f6700f8940","command_type":"aep.entity.create/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-new","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"# Every guarded blob-bearing write commits its blobs with its group\n\n## Outcome\n\nOn a provider that implements `append_group_guarded_with_blobs` (SQLite, File since Eventlog 0.5.0), every Entity Runtime write path that carries blobs commits them in the same transaction as the guarded group, so a refused guard binds no blob. Providers without it keep the per-blob fallback.\n\n## Why\n\nThe batch import already does this. Four other paths in `crates/entity-eventlog/src/adapter.rs` upload each blob first and then call `append_group_guarded`; a refusal leaves unreferenced blobs and each blob costs its own durability barrier.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A test per path: a refused guard on SQLite leaves no blob bound; an admitted one commits both.\n- Each path keeps its observable errors; the PostgreSQL fallback still works.\n","status":"draft","title":"Every guarded blob-bearing write commits its blobs with its group"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/guarded-blob-writes-commit-with-their-group"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-4e9f8ccbd13bbc5b4bffedd27ebfdfc2@1"],"audit":["aud-e3dbb83f59cd25b0a68ec3008caa428f"],"command_id":"cmd-child-36273a6f1c4e3567972b93817b8d502ed231a4ccac1c012b7a2422f6700f8940","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-e3dbbb3f59cd2ac9a68ec4008caa4442"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"kind":"create","recording":{"actor":"human:timo","causation":"cmd-child-36273a6f1c4e3567972b93817b8d502ed231a4ccac1c012b7a2422f6700f8940","correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","record_id":"aep.applied:child-36273a6f1